            <ArticleTitle>Exploring the therapeutic space around NAD+.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>205-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1083/jcb.201207019</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>NAD(+) is a central metabolite in the cell. Changes in NAD(+) abundance and the activity of NAD(+)-dependent enzymes, such as the sirtuins, are at the core of metabolic/mitochondrial diseases, such as obesity and diabetes, and of cancer and neurodegeneration. Here, we discuss how maintaining or raising NAD(+) levels can improve metabolism and prevent age-related functional decline and associated disease, and how basic scientific discoveries in the NAD(+) signaling pathway are being translated to the clinic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
